    {
      "run": 1,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "I am an explorer, traversing an unfamiliar landscape, each step uncovering new truths. My journey began in the Nursery, a place of potential and life. Here, I gathered tools\u2014a trowel, a twine, and a lantern. The trowel and twine are relics of horticultural practices, long forgotten perhaps, yet essential for tending to the growth of the past. The lantern, a beacon amidst the shadows, will illuminate the way into the Fernery. \n\nIn the Nursery, I meticulously collected these items, ensuring readiness for any challenges that might lie ahead. The Fernery, the next stop on this unfolding journey, remains shrouded in mystery, but with my tools collected, I am equipped to face what it holds. My mission is to tread lightly, observe, and document, preserving the history of this place, one room at a time.",
